<!-- =========================================
     03 / RESEARCH FINDINGS
========================================= -->
<section class="project-section nf-findings-section"
         id="insights">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="row justify-content-center text-center mb-5">
      <div class="col-lg-9">
        <p class="description">03 / Research Findings</p>

        <h2>What We Discovered</h2>

        <p>
          By connecting qualitative research with website,
          market, and behavioural analysis, we identified
          four priorities for improving how professional
          visitors evaluate Neurofit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Finding 01 -->
    <article class="nf-finding">
      <div class="row align-items-center g-5">

        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <p class="description">01 / VALUE CLARITY</p>

          <h3>The Offering Was Difficult to Evaluate Quickly</h3>

          <p>
            Interview participants needed clearer explanations
            of Neurofit's features, supported applications,
            and practical use within professional workflows.
            The website audit also identified weaknesses in
            the value proposition and content hierarchy.
          </p>

          <p class="nf-finding-implication">
            <strong>Design Implication</strong><br>
            Explain the offering earlier, using concise
            value statements and concrete workflow examples.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <div class="nf-evidence-card">
            <span>SUPPORTING EVIDENCE</span>

            <p>
              Interview themes + website content audit
            </p>

            <div class="nf-evidence-placeholder">
              Insert annotated original website screenshot
              or research evidence.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Finding 02 -->
    <article class="nf-finding">
      <div class="row align-items-center g-5">

        <div class="col-lg-5 order-1 order-lg-2">
          <p class="description">02 / FINDABILITY</p>

          <h3>Navigation Labels Created Uncertainty</h3>

          <p>
            Both participants navigated toward "Use Cases"
            during tree testing but expressed uncertainty
            about the label. Card sorting also revealed
            different expectations for grouping professional
            information and supporting resources.
          </p>

          <p class="nf-finding-implication">
            <strong>Design Implication</strong><br>
            Clarify navigation terminology, reduce
            unnecessary hierarchy, and organize content
            around audience expectations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7 order-2 order-lg-1">
          <div class="nf-evidence-card">
            <span>SUPPORTING EVIDENCE</span>

            <p>
              Tree-testing observations + card-sorting patterns
            </p>

            <div class="nf-evidence-placeholder">
              Insert tree-testing paths or an anonymized
              card-sorting visualization.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Finding 03 -->
    <article class="nf-finding">
      <div class="row align-items-center g-5">

        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <p class="description">03 / AUDIENCE RELEVANCE</p>

          <h3>Different Audiences Needed Different Evidence</h3>

          <p>
            Clinicians focused on clinical applications,
            supported diagnoses, workflow integration,
            and outcomes. Insurance and TPA stakeholders
            prioritized return-to-work outcomes, reporting
            capabilities, and organizational credibility.
          </p>

          <p class="nf-finding-implication">
            <strong>Design Implication</strong><br>
            Provide clear audience-specific pathways
            while maintaining a coherent overall
            product narrative.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <div class="nf-audience-comparison">

            <div class="nf-audience-card">
              <span>CLINICIANS</span>
              <h4>Clinical Fit</h4>
              <p>
                Supported diagnoses, activity examples,
                workflow integration, clinical outcomes.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="nf-audience-card">
              <span>INSURERS &amp; TPAs</span>
              <h4>Operational Value</h4>
              <p>
                Return-to-work outcomes, reporting previews,
                implementation considerations, credibility.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Finding 04 -->
    <article class="nf-finding">
      <div class="row align-items-center g-5">

        <div class="col-lg-5 order-1 order-lg-2">
          <p class="description">04 / TRUST &amp; CREDIBILITY</p>

          <h3>Credibility Needed to Come Before Conversion</h3>

          <p>
            Participants emphasized the importance of
            case studies, testimonials, clinical evidence,
            professional background, and transparent
            information when evaluating the offering.
          </p>

          <p>
            Competitive research also suggested that
            differentiation depended on communicating
            value and outcomes more clearly, rather
            than simply adding more authority claims.
          </p>

          <p class="nf-finding-implication">
            <strong>Design Implication</strong><br>
            Surface relevant proof throughout the
            evaluation journey and align calls to action
            with visitors' readiness to proceed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7 order-2 order-lg-1">
          <div class="nf-evidence-card">
            <span>SUPPORTING EVIDENCE</span>

            <p>
              Interview themes + competitive positioning
              analysis + website audit
            </p>

            <div class="nf-evidence-placeholder">
              Insert selected competitive analysis excerpt
              or trust-signal audit evidence.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>


<!-- =========================================
     04 / FROM RESEARCH TO DESIGN STRATEGY
========================================= -->
<section class="project-section nf-strategy-section"
         id="design-strategy">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="row justify-content-center text-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9">

        <p class="description">
          04 / From Research to Design Strategy
        </p>

        <h2>Trust Before Conversion</h2>

        <p class="nf-strategy-intro">
          Our research suggested that supporting conversion
          required more than prominent calls to action.
          Professional visitors first needed to understand
          Neurofit's value, find information relevant to
          their needs, and evaluate credible evidence.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4 mt-3">

      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="nf-strategy-card">
          <span>01 / CLARITY</span>
          <h3>Explain the Value</h3>
          <p>
            Communicate what Neurofit offers,
            how it works, and why it matters.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="nf-strategy-card">
          <span>02 / RELEVANCE</span>
          <h3>Guide Each Audience</h3>
          <p>
            Create clear pathways for clinicians
            and insurance stakeholders.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="nf-strategy-card">
          <span>03 / CREDIBILITY</span>
          <h3>Build Confidence</h3>
          <p>
            Make supporting evidence accessible
            before asking visitors to take action.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center mt-5">
      <div class="col-lg-9 text-center">
        <p class="nf-strategy-outcome">
          These priorities informed our approach to
          information architecture, content hierarchy,
          interface design, and conversion pathways.
          Improved conversion remained a business goal,
          not a measured outcome of this research phase.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

